The attached image (Figure 2) illustrates the in vivo kinetics of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles in mice. Panel (a) shows whole-animal fluorescence imaging over 21 days, indicating Nano-11 is retained at the injection site and gradually clears. Panel (b) confirms minimal systemic distribution by day 21, as no fluorescence is detected in major internal organs. Panel (c) quantifies the fluorescence intensity at the injection site, demonstrating a significant decrease over time, consistent with Nano-11's transient presence and effective clearance from the injection site, supporting its potential as a safe vaccine adjuvant.